IShoppingMallInventoryUnit.description:
Core inventory unit tracking available stock for each product variant.

Represents the current available stock quantity for a specific product variant owned by a seller. This is the authoritative source for stock availability during checkout operations.

Each record corresponds to one unique product variant and contains the current available quantity after all reservations and allocations have been accounted for.

The inventory unit record is created when a seller adds a new product variant to their inventory and is used to validate stock availability during order processing. All inventory changes are tracked in inventory_transactions for audit purposes.

This entity directly maps to the shopping_mall_inventory_units Prisma model and contains all fields from that table except for internal system fields.

@link shopping_mall_product_variants.id
@link shopping_mall_sellers.id
@link shopping_mall_inventory_transactions.type 'adjusted' --record of inventory changes
@link shopping_mall_inventory_alerts --triggered when quantity falls below min_stock_threshold

Used in: POST /shoppingMall/seller/inventory/units (response), PUT /shoppingMall/seller/inventory/units/{unitId} (response)

IShoppingMallInventoryAlert.description:
Inventory alert entity representing when inventory levels fall below configured thresholds.

Represents system-generated notifications for inventory units whose current stock quantity drops below min_stock_threshold. Alerts are created when inventory falls below threshold and cleared when inventory increases above threshold.

This entity links to specific inventory units and their associated sellers, providing visibility into stock condition events across the marketplace. Alert types indicate severity level: 'low_stock', 'critical_stock', or 'back_in_stock'.

The entity includes full details of the alert event including the threshold value, current stock quantity, and timestamps for generation and clearance.

Used in detailed alert retrieval operations (GET /shoppingMall/inventory/alerts/{alertId}).

